<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2017/Blooming-Hill-Farm3.jpg" alt="An oil painting of a lavender farm by artist Simon Bland" width="650" height="485" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Lavender Farm. 9x12, oil on linen panel. 2015</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">A plein air painting done this morning at Blooming Hill Farm in Purcellville, VA. It was a lovely day to be painting outside and I couldn't get the paint down fast enough, even with a large palette knife, to keep up with the movement of the sky.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">While finishing up I picked nearly 40 flies off the painting then proceeded to drop it face down on the lawn. This required more than a few minutes of careful brush work to fix, after which the whole easel and palette promptly fell on top of a tree peony.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">Despite this, the battle scars were mostly fixed on site&mdash;those that are left serve as a reminder that this is a true plein air painting.</span></p>